Subject: Record native allocation ownership beneath the original free-list allocator
Upstream-base: dc238202b310059d80791d0140dee37f27b9a3bf

Retain the original allocation/free ring, payload and ordering decisions. Host
ownership records distinguish overlapping parent/custom heaps and retain the
actual allocator after its source stack entry is popped. Reserve host metadata
before original ring mutation; record successful start/end allocations, validate
exact native frees and retire metadata after genuine free/reset/backing release.
No game managers, source readiness, ordinary global operators or shutdown flow
are replaced. Native metadata locks do not qualify concurrent mutation of the
original allocator or CurrentAllocator/AllocatorStack.

